			"notes": "Portable source-checkout ports for Fabric and NeoForge, for developers with a Gradle source project.\n\n## What this beta does\n\n- Ports a mod between Minecraft versions within its loader, with a reversible edit set, a packaged build and a mixin audit.\n- Verified this round: Fabric F3Nope/AppleSkin 1.21.5 <-> 1.21.6; NeoForge ZombieApocalypseAddon 1.21.1 -> 1.21.4 with no hand edits (75s cold, 14s repeated), the ported jar loads in a real 1.21.4 client and its /za command runs.\n- Stops with named errors instead of guessing: 1.21.1 -> 1.21.6 leaves 9 semantic items; Jade 1.21.1 -> 1.21.6 leaves the 1.21.6 GUI rewrite.\n- Real game checks: ui-check, world-check, --expect-change, --save-roundtrip, with inspected 1280x720 captures.\n- Safe undo, verified dependency resolution, and a receipt (result.json) with stage timings from every command.\n\n## What it does not do\n\n- It does not change a mod's loader. Fabric stays Fabric, NeoForge stays NeoForge.\n- Compiled JARs are not accepted; a Gradle source checkout with its wrapper is required.\n- Multi-project/Stonecutter and Kotlin sources are partial or untested.\n\n## Install\n\nDownload the portable ZIP, check it against the .sha256, extract it and run `./modaccel support` (Windows: `modaccel.cmd support`). Java 17+ is required; on Windows a missing runtime is downloaded and verified once.\n\nWindows, Linux and macOS run the portable checks in hosted CI; game checks are verified on Windows only."
		}
